1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,950
Don Giovanni, episode ten: the stone guest.

2
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:14,950
Candles, a laid table, a little band playing the hits of the day, and then a tune Leporello knows only too well, from The Marriage of Figaro. Leporello steals pheasant. Ah, what a barbarous appetite, laughs his master.

3
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:25,970
Donna Elvira bursts in and kneels. She asks only that he change his life. He laughs, and drinks: long live women, long live good wine! She goes to the door, and screams. She runs out the other way.

4
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:41,500
Leporello looks out and comes back white. The stone man, he says. Ta ta ta ta: those are his steps. A knock. Leporello hides under the table. The Commendatore fills the doorway. Don Giovanni, you invited me to supper, and I have come. Will you come to supper with me? Don Giovanni does not run. I will come.

5
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:47,410
Give me your hand on it. He gives it. What cold is this? Repent! No! Repent! No! The statue lets go.

6
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:57,790
Fire comes from every side, the floor opens, a chorus from below: all this is little for your crimes. Who is tearing my soul? he cries. Don Giovanni goes down into the abyss.

7
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:11,580
The others come too late. Donna Anna asks Ottavio for one more year. Elvira goes to a convent. Zerlina and Masetto go home to dinner. Leporello, to the inn, to find a better master. And all of them sing: this is the end of those who do evil.
